# C8 reduced TS, FINAL: full-system OptTS Freq (no ActiveAtoms), TightOpt.
#
# ActiveAtoms was SCAFFOLDING. It took the optimiser from a poor full-system
# start to a frozen-host saddle, which is how we got a good geometry at all --
# but a barrier must be made of one model, and the RC (../rc/) is a full
# 137-atom relaxation. A frozen-host TS against a fully-relaxed RC mixes two
# models and is not the number to publish. Here the whole system relaxes.
#
# Seed: the frozen-host TightOpt TS (../optts_freq_tight/job.xyz). Its QM region
# is already at the saddle, which is what makes the full search tractable -- the
# 2026-09-19 attempts that would not converge started from far worse geometries.
#
# No ActiveAtoms and no ExtendActiveRegion: %qmmm QMATOMS defines the QM1 region
# only. The Hessian is therefore full-system (409 displacements), so this is
# slower than the frozen-host runs by roughly the host's share of the system.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  MaxIter 400
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
